NAME
       strerror, strsignal, perror - describe an error

SYNOPSIS
       #include <string.h>
       #include <stdio.h>

       char *strerror(int errnum);
       char *strsignal(int sig);
       void  perror(const char *s);

DESCRIPTION
       strerror returns the text for an errno value and strsignal the
       name of a signal. perror writes S, a colon and the text of the
       current errno to standard error.

RETURN VALUE
       A pointer to a static string that the next call may overwrite.

SEE ALSO
       errno(3), err(3)
